Raise the recursion limit for the chatgpt crate.

rustc computes the layout of the async fn body in connectors::list_connectors
at a query depth 130 above the default limit of 128, and aborts with "queries
overflow the depth limit". Upstream does not hit this because it pins rustc
1.95.0 in rust-toolchain.toml; the limit is reached with 1.98.

Upstream already applies exactly this attribute to its other crates that grew
past the limit -- tui, exec, app-server and the goal extension's tests -- so
this extends that treatment to chatgpt rather than inventing a workaround.

--- a/chatgpt/src/lib.rs
+++ b/chatgpt/src/lib.rs
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+#![recursion_limit = "256"]
+
 pub mod apply_command;
 mod chatgpt_client;
 pub mod connectors;
